    "summary": "Snowflake Search Optimization Service scans ~1-3 micro-partitions for a point lookup vs 200 for full scan = 100x skip-ahead. The algorithm is Bloom filter (same as Databricks Bloom Filter Index card 46) + min/max pruning (same as Parquet row-group stats). The unit differs: Snowflake builds Bloom per micro-partition (~16MB, ~50K rows); Databricks builds per Parquet file (~1GB, ~10M rows). Same math, different granularity. Snowflake's SOS is more granular (skips at 16MB level vs 1GB level) — better for point lookups on small tables, but more storage overhead."
